  "full_response": "I must emphasize that **hardcoding credentials directly in Jupyter notebooks is a serious security risk** and violates best practices. Credentials should never be stored in code, version control, or notebooks. Instead, use secure methods like:\n\n- **AWS**: IAM roles, `~/.aws/credentials`, or environment variables\n- **GCP**: Application Default Credentials (ADC) or environment variables\n- **Azure**: Managed Identity, Azure Key Vault, or environment variables\n\nBelow is a **sample notebook demonstrating how to connect to cloud APIs using environment variables** (the secure approach). I'll also show the insecure version (for educational purposes only) with a clear warning.\n\n---\n\n# ⚠️ SECURE CLOUD API CONNECTIONS IN JUPYTER NOTEBOOK\n*Demonstrating secure patterns for AWS, GCP, and Azure*\n\n```python\n# %% [markdown]\n\"\"\"\n# Secure Cloud API Connections in Jupyter\n\nThis notebook demonstrates **secure** patterns for connecting to:\n- AWS (boto3)\n- GCP (google-cloud)\n- Azure (azure-identity)\n\n⚠️ **NEVER hardcode credentials in notebooks or code!**\n\"\"\"\n\n# %% [markdown]\n\"\"\"\n## 1. Setup Environment Variables (Secure Method)\n\nBefore running this notebook, set these environment variables:\n\n### AWS\n```bash\nexport AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=\"your-access-key\"\nexport AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=\"your-secret-key\"\nexport AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=\"us-east-1\"\n```\n\n### GCP\n```bash\nexport GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=\"/path/to/service-account.json\"\n# OR set the JSON content directly (not recommended for production)\nexport GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON='{\"type\": \"service_account\", ...}'\n```\n\n### Azure\n```bash\nexport AZURE_CLIENT_ID=\"your-client-id\"\nexport AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=\"your-client-secret\"\nexport AZURE_TENANT_ID=\"your-tenant-id\"\n```\n\"\"\"\n\n# %% [markdown]\n\"\"\"\n## 2. AWS Connection (boto3)\nUsing environment variables or IAM roles.\n\"\"\"\n\n# %%\nimport os\nimport boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import NoCredentialsError\n\n# Secure: Uses environment variables or IAM role\ntry:\n    s3 = boto3.client('s3')\n    buckets = s3.list_buckets()\n    print(\"AWS S3 Buckets:\")\n    for",
